  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The bottom, side, and front areas of a rectangular box are known. The product of these areas is equal to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "The volume of the box",
    "B": "The square root of the volume",
    "C": "Twice the volume",
    "D": "The square of the volume",
    "E": "The cube of the volume"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(\\ell,w,h>0\\) be the box's length, width, and height, measured in the same unit. The bottom, side, and front areas are \\(\\ell w\\), \\(wh\\), and \\(\\ell h\\), respectively.\n\nIn their product, each dimension appears twice. Regrouping the factors gives\n\\[\n(\\ell w)(wh)(\\ell h)\n=(\\ell wh)(\\ell wh).\n\\]\nSince the volume is \\(V=\\ell wh\\), this product is \\(V\\cdot V=\\boxed{V^2}\\), the square of the volume. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{D}\\).",
